# Python Security

- Secrets come from environment / vault — never hardcode tokens or passwords.
- Do not log JWT secrets, passwords, Fernet keys, or session plaintext.
- Validate authz server-side on every sensitive route; UI hiding is not security.
- Prefer existing bcrypt/PyJWT/cryptography usage; do not invent crypto.
- For django-security skill references in upstream ECC: **N/A** — this is FastAPI.
- See skills `security-review`, `vault-fernet-sessions`, `tenant-isolation-max`.
